Propellerhead Remote Mapping File
File Format Version	1.0.0
Control Surface Manufacturer	Akai
Control Surface Model	MPK Mini Play
Map Version	1.0.0


//======================================================================
//  Rytmik Drum Machine
//
//  Pads 1-8   -> Drum 1-8 Mute       (Bank A)
//  Pads 9-16  -> Drum 1-8 Solo       (Bank B)
//  Knobs 1-4A -> Drum 1-4 Volume     (CC21-24)
//  Knobs 1-4B -> Drum 5-8 Volume     (CC25-28)
//  Joystick X -> (no pitch bend; retargetable via override)
//  Joystick Y -> (no mod wheel; retargetable via override)
//  Keyboard   -> Keyboard
//
//  NOTE: Rytmik is a Reason Compact-derived device, so its remote
//  item names use underscores (Drum_1_Volume, Master_Volume etc.)
//  and its scope is se.propellerheads.DMFC.
//======================================================================

Scope	Propellerhead Software	se.propellerheads.DMFC
// Define Group	Keyboard Shortcut Variations	Level	FX
//	Control Surface Item	Key	Remotable Item	Scale	Mode

Map	_Scope		"Rytmik"
Map	Keyboard		Keyboard

// --- Pads (Bank A): mute per channel -----------------
Map	Pad 1		Drum_1_Mute
Map	Pad 2		Drum_2_Mute
Map	Pad 3		Drum_3_Mute
Map	Pad 4		Drum_4_Mute
Map	Pad 5		Drum_5_Mute
Map	Pad 6		Drum_6_Mute
Map	Pad 7		Drum_7_Mute
Map	Pad 8		Drum_8_Mute

// --- Pads (Bank B): solo per channel -----------------
Map	Pad 9		Drum_1_Solo
Map	Pad 10		Drum_2_Solo
Map	Pad 11		Drum_3_Solo
Map	Pad 12		Drum_4_Solo
Map	Pad 13		Drum_5_Solo
Map	Pad 14		Drum_6_Solo
Map	Pad 15		Drum_7_Solo
Map	Pad 16		Drum_8_Solo

// --- Knob Bank A (CC21-24): channel levels 1-4 -------
Map	Knob 1 A		Drum_1_Volume
Map	Knob 2 A		Drum_2_Volume
Map	Knob 3 A		Drum_3_Volume
Map	Knob 4 A		Drum_4_Volume

// --- Knob Bank B (CC25-28): channel levels 5-8 -------
Map	Knob 1 B		Drum_5_Volume
Map	Knob 2 B		Drum_6_Volume
Map	Knob 3 B		Drum_7_Volume
Map	Knob 4 B		Drum_8_Volume

// --- Joystick / wheels -------------------------------
// Rytmik exposes neither pitch bend nor mod wheel. The lines below are
// deliberately left commented; use Remote Overrides to re-point them to
// Master_Pitch / Master_Reverb / Master_Filter if desired.
//Map	Joystick X		Master_Pitch
//Map	Joystick Y		Master_Reverb